          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Ordinary differential cohomology is the
            = succeed "-refinement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
          %p
            Every
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %em ordinary differential cohomology
            one refers, for emphasis, to the differential refinement of
            %em
              ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            , hence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            represented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(-,\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            is often just called
            %em cohomology
            when the context is clear,
            %em ordinary differential cohomology
            is often called just
            %em differential cohomology
            \.
          %p
            Ordinary differential cohomology classifies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle"} circle bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundles"} principal 2-bundles
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} 2-connection
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Here we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{diff}^\bullet(X)
            for the ordinary differential cohomology groups of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#CurvatureAndCharClass Curvature and characteristic class
          %p
            There are two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
            morphisms:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi diff
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      c : H_{diff}^\bullet(X) \to H^\bullet(X,\mathbb{Z})
              %p
                produces the class in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
                that underlies a differential cocycle;
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi diff
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{diff}(X)
                    this is called the first
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
                    of a
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
                %li
                  %p
                    for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi diff
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3_{diff}(X)
                    this is called the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dixmier-Douady+class"} Dixmier-Douady class
                    of the corresponding
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi diff
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi cl
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      F : H_{diff}^\bullet(X) \to \Omega^\bullet_{cl}(X)
              %p
                produces a closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                of degree
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/period"} period
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#AbstractProperties"} below
          %p
            The following is either a definition, if regarded as an axiomatic characterization of ordinary differential cohomology, or it is a proposition, if regarded as a property of one of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Models"} models
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi diff
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{diff}^n(X)
                for the ordinary differential cohomology of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                in degree
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n-1}(X)
                for the collection of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi int
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n-1}_{int}(X)
                for the collection of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                of degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
                that are closed and whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periods"} periods
                are integral: for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \colon S^{n-1} \to X
                we have the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mi γ
                          %mo *
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{S^{n-1}} \gamma^* \omega \in \mathbb{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi int
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^n_{int}(X)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(X, \mathbb{Z})
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n\big(X, U(1)\big)
                for the ordinary cohomology (for instance modeled as
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                with coefficients in the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                (regarded as a
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
          %p
            All of these sets are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %a{:href => "#CurvatureAndCharClass"} above
            are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          #ExactSequencesForOrdDiffCohomology.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The differential cohomology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{diff}^n(X)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              fits into
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequences"} short exact sequences
              of abelian groups
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong curvature exact sequence
                #eq:CurvatureSequence.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi diff
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi F
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi int
                            %mo ,
                            %mi clsd
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        0 \to H^{n-1}\big(X, U(1)\big) \to H^n_{diff}(X) \stackrel{F}{\to} \Omega_{int, clsd}^n(X) \to 0
              %li
                %p
                  %strong characteristic class exact sequence
                #eq:CharacteristicClassSequence.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi int
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi diff
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi c
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        0
                        \\to
                        \\Omega^{n-1}(X)/\Omega^{n-1}_{int}(X)
                        \\to
                        H_{diff}^n(X)
                        \\stackrel{c}{\to}
                        H^n(X, \mathbb{Z})
                        \\to
                        0
                        \\,.
          %p
            The first sequence
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CurvatureSequence"} (1)
            says in words: two circle
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            coincides differ by a
            %em flat
            circle (n-1)-bundle.
          %p
            The second sequence
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CharacteristicClassSequence"} (2)
            says in words: two connections on the same circle
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "-form," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %p
            More is true: both these sequences interlock to form the hexagonal
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
            of ordinary differential cohomology. For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+cohomology+diagram#DeligneCoefficients"} differential cohomology diagram – Examples – Deligne coefficients
          %h3#Models Models
          %p
            There are various equivalent
            = succeed "-models" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheeger-Simons+differential+character"}> Cheeger-Simons differential character
                s;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"}> Deligne cohomology
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"}> circle n-bundles with connection
                \.
          %p
            The last of these are often known as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
          %p
            Cocycles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \in H_{diff}^2(X)
            in degree 2 ordinary differential cohomology are represented by ordinary
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(\nabla) \in H^2(X,\mathbb{Z})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
            of the underlying circle bundle and the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\nabla \in \Omega^2_{cl}(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form of the connection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
          %h2#fiber_integration Fiber integration
          %p see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#in_chernweil_theory In Chern-Weil theory
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle
            of degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
            may be refined to a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^1(X,G) \to H_{diff}^{2n}(X)
          %p
            from the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            classifying
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
            ordinary differential cohomology.
          %p The projection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^1(X,G) \to H_{diff}^{2n}(X) \stackrel{c}{\to} H^{2n}(X,\mathbb{Z})
          %p
            is the integral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            corresponding to the invariant polynomial and the projection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^1(X,G) \to H_{diff}^{2n}(X) \stackrel{F}{\to} \Omega^{2n}_{cl}(X)
          %p
            is a differential form which represents the image of this class under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{2n}(X,\mathbb{Z}) \to H^{2n}(X,\mathbb{R})
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            (under the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
          %h3#in_physics In physics
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
                is a cocycle in degree 2 ordinary differential cohomology
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kalb-Ramond+field"} Kalb-Ramond field
                is a cocycle in degree 3;
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
                is a cocycle in degree 4.
          %p
            In abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (4k+3)
            a field configuration is a cocycle in ordinary differential geometry of degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2k+2)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
          %h2#in_a_general_abstract_context In a general abstract context
          %p
            Ordinary differential cohomology (and indeed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            model thereof) is defined generally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cohesive%20%28infinity,1%29-topos%20--%20structures#DifferentialCohomology"}> cohesive (∞,1)-topos – structures – differential cohomology
              \.
          %p
            For the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            this intrinsic definition reproduces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
            model. This is discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/smooth%20infinity-groupoid%20--%20structures#StrucDifferentialCohomology"} Smooth∞Grpd – structures – differential cohomology
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} twisted ordinary differential cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} equivariant ordinary differential cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+Chow+group"} arithmetic Chow group
          %h2#references References
          %p For more and more original references see:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheeger-Simons+differential+characters"} Cheeger-Simons differential characters
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Byungdo+Park"}> Byungdo Park
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential cohomology and gerbes: An introduction to higher differential geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://byungdo.github.io/seminars/IMSRS.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Park-DifferentialCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (emphasis on relation to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle+gerbe"} with connection
          %p
            For discussion in the broader context of generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            see
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2Cand+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology,and M-Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0211216"}> arXiv
                )
              %ul
                %li
                  %p A pedestrian introduction of ordinary differential cocycles is in section 2.3 there.
                %li
                  %p
                    The systematic construction and definition via a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
                    is in section 3.2.
                %li
                  %p The relation to Chern-Weil theory is in section 3.3.
          %p A characterization by the two characteristic exact sequences is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"}> James Simons
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axiomatic characterization of ordinary differential cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0701077"} arXiv:math/0701077
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/jtopol/jtm006"} doi:10.1112/jtopol/jtm006
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://jtopol.oxfordjournals.org/content/1/1/45.full.pdf+html"} web pdf
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} equivariant ordinary differential cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernesto+Lupercio"}> Ernesto Lupercio
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"} Bernardo Uribe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deligne Cohomology for Orbifolds, discrete torsion and B-fields
                %em Geometric and topological methods for quantum field theory
                Proceedings, Summer School, Villa de Leyva, Colombia, July 9-27, 2001 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201184"}> arXiv:hep-th/0201184
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/582101"} spire:582101
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"}> Kiyonori Gomi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant smooth Deligne cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ojm/1153494380"} euclid:ojm/1153494380
            %li
              %p
                Andreas Kübel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Thom"} Andreas Thom
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant Differential Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/tran/7315"} doi:10.1090/tran/7315
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.06392"} arXiv:1510.06392
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Corbett+Redden"}> Corbett Redden
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Borel equivariant cohomology via connections
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://nyjm.albany.edu/j/2017/23-20.html"} nyjm:23-20
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.06921"} arXiv:1602.06921
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Corbett+Redden"}> Corbett Redden
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An alternate description of equivariant connections
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.difgeo.2017.11.003"} doi:10.1016/j.difgeo.2017.11.003
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.01297"} arXiv:1608.01297
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Byungdo+Park"}> Byungdo Park
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Corbett+Redden"} Corbett Redden
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A classification of equivariant gerbe connections
                %strong 21
                02 1850001 (2019) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0219199718500013"}> doi:10.1142/S0219199718500013
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Cheng-Yong Du Xiaojuan Zhao,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spark and Deligne-Beilinson cohomology on orbifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2016.02.011"} doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2016.02.011
            %li
              %p
                Cheng-Yong Du, Lili Shen, Xiaojuan Zhao,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spark complexes on good effective orbifold atlases categorically
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/33/26/33-26abs.html"} tac:33-26
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.07551"} arXiv:1708.07551
          %p
            Discussion of variants of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+concretification"} differentially concretified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            (higher
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes+with+connection"} bundle gerbes with connection
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Severin+Bunk"}> Severin Bunk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+S.+Shahbazi"} Carlos S. Shahbazi
              %em Higher Geometric Structures on Manifolds and the Gauge Theory of Deligne Cohomology
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06633"}> arXiv:2304.06633
              \&amp;rbrack;
